  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 375°F. Line a baking sheet pan with parchment paper.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Cut cheese slices into quarters. Set aside. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 slice cheddar cheese, sliced"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place sausages on a microwave-safe plate and heat on high until just warmed through, about 1 minute. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "8 turkey breakfast sausage patties, fully cooked"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, remove 4 biscuits from the package. Using your fingers, separate the top from the bottom portion of each biscuit and arrange on the baking sheet, opened-side facing up. Top each biscuit half with a quarter slice of cheese, a warmed sausage patty, and a second piece of cheese. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (453 g) tube biscuit dough"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Separate remaining biscuits, then cover the \"sandwiches\" (with the open-side facing down), and press edges to seal.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking sheet in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and bake until the biscuits are cooked through and golden, about 15 minutes. Remove from oven.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash, dry, and chop (or tear) lettuce into bite-sized pieces. Place in a medium bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, and halve grape tomatoes. Add to the bowl with the lettuce, along with dressing, and toss to combine the salad.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 pint grape tomatoes\n⅓ cup ranch dressing"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide sandwiches and salad between plates. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
